        <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl lg:text-4xl text-ink leading-tight mb-5">Mental Health Support for International Students in Famagusta</h1>
        <p class="text-ink-muted text-lg leading-relaxed">Studying abroad is one of the most exciting decisions you can make — and one of the most challenging. For thousands of international students in Famagusta, the distance from home brings unique psychological pressures that the campus rarely talks about.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-12 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <div class="prose-custom space-y-8">

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">The reality of studying abroad in North Cyprus</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Famagusta is home to several universities, including Near East University's affiliated campuses, attracting students from over 100 countries. While the Mediterranean climate and multicultural environment create a vibrant student life, they also bring a set of psychological challenges that many students are unprepared for.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Unlike domestic students who can return home for a weekend, international students often go months without seeing family or close friends. Add to this a new language, unfamiliar academic expectations, financial pressure and cultural differences — and the foundations for a mental health crisis are in place.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-primary/5 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-primary/15">
            <p class="text-sm text-ink font-medium mb-2">By the numbers</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Research consistently shows that international students experience higher rates of depression, anxiety and loneliness than their domestic peers. A 2023 meta-analysis found that approximately 1 in 3 international students meets the clinical threshold for an anxiety or depressive disorder during their studies.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Common mental health struggles for international students</h2>
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Culture shock and identity confusion</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Moving between cultures can destabilise your sense of identity. You may feel "too foreign" in Famagusta and "too changed" when you go home. This in-between experience is common — and it passes — but it can feel very disorienting in the moment.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Loneliness and homesickness</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Homesickness is not "weakness" — it is a natural grief response to meaningful separation. Many students feel pressure to appear fine in front of new peers while struggling privately. Social media can make it worse, offering a curated highlight reel of friends' lives back home.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Academic pressure and performance anxiety</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">International students often carry enormous expectations — from families, sponsors and themselves. Studying in a second or third language intensifies this pressure. A single poor grade can feel catastrophic when financial and visa status depend on academic standing.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Financial stress and precarity</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Currency fluctuations, limited work permits and dependence on remittances create a backdrop of financial anxiety that many students manage silently. This chronic low-grade stress has significant mental health consequences over time.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">What professional support looks like</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Talking to a psychologist is not a sign that something is "seriously wrong." It is a proactive investment in your wellbeing — the same way going to the gym is an investment in your physical health.</p>
            <ul class="space-y-3">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">A safe, confidential space</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Everything you share stays between you and your psychologist. There is no judgement, no reporting to your university, no consequences for your academic status.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Practical coping strategies</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">You will not spend sessions just venting. Evidence-based therapies like CBT equip you with tools you can use immediately — for exam stress, low mood, relationship conflict and more.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Support without time pressure</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Unlike a brief drop-in at a campus counselling office, regular therapy sessions allow you to work through issues in depth, at your own pace.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">How Mağusa Psikoloji supports international students</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">We offer English-language therapy sessions in Famagusta, designed around the specific challenges international students face. Our approach is warm, non-judgmental and culturally sensitive.</p>
            <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-2">What we offer</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1.5">
                  <li>• Sessions fully in English</li>
                  <li>• Flexible afternoon and evening appointments</li>
                  <li>• Online sessions available</li>
                  <li>• Anxiety, depression, exam stress, identity</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-2">Who we work with</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1.5">
                  <li>• University students and graduates</li>
                  <li>• METU NCC students</li>
                  <li>• Postgraduate and PhD researchers</li>
                  <li>• International staff and families</li>
                  <li>• Anyone living in Famagusta</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">How to access therapy as a university student in Famagusta</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Finding a psychologist in Famagusta as a university student is simpler than many students expect. Here is how it works at Mağusa Psikoloji Centre:</p>
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <div class="flex gap-4 items-start">
                <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-primary flex items-center justify-center text-white text-sm font-bold shrink-0">1</div>
                <div>
                  <p class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1">Message us on WhatsApp</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">No referral needed. No waiting list. Send a brief message introducing yourself and what you are looking for — in English or Turkish.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="flex gap-4 items-start">
                <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-primary flex items-center justify-center text-white text-sm font-bold shrink-0">2</div>
                <div>
                  <p class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1">Book your first session</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">We'll confirm your preferred format (in-person or online), find a time that works around your timetable, and send you everything you need ahead of your first session.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="flex gap-4 items-start">
                <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-primary flex items-center justify-center text-white text-sm font-bold shrink-0">3</div>
                <div>
                  <p class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1">Choose in-person or online</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Sessions are available at our Famagusta centre or online. Online sessions are popular with students living on campus or in shared accommodation where privacy can be limited.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="flex gap-4 items-start">
                <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-primary flex items-center justify-center text-white text-sm font-bold shrink-0">4</div>
                <div>
                  <p class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1">Flexible scheduling around your timetable</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">We offer morning, afternoon and evening slots. Sessions are completely confidential — nothing is shared with your university, department or any third party.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-accent/5 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-accent/15">
            <p class="text-sm text-ink font-medium mb-2">You do not have to be in crisis to come</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Many students wait until they are struggling severely before reaching out. But therapy is most effective when you start early — before problems become entrenched. If something feels off, that is enough of a reason to book a conversation.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
